    {
      "id": "07d4753aafe7dc46464a7ab8cc75c7085240da46",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1286011720,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "This broke the build for me, Debian bullseye, clang 11.0.1, Qt 5.15.2:\n\n```\n../ui/qt/models/packet_list_model.cpp:344:40: error: implicit conversion loses integer precision: 'qsizetype' (aka 'long long') to 'int' [-Werror,-Wshorten-64-to-32]\n        const auto &index = indices.at(i);\n                                    ~~ ^\n../ui/qt/models/packet_list_model.cpp:419:40: error: implicit conversion loses integer precision: 'qsizetype' (aka 'long long') to 'int' [-Werror,-Wshorten-64-to-32]\n        const auto &index = indices.at(i);\n                                    ~~ ^\n```\n\nSeems the `QList::size` return value and `QList::at` argument were `int` in Qt5 but `qsizetype` in Qt6. Why did this not fail in CI? Do we have no Qt5 runner?",
          "author": {
            "id": 620868,
            "username": "nicolas17",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Nicolás Alvarez",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/82fc14a8d756131416a2f108bbdd6009b2ba9df642adc22729ba38ca05c8cc00?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/nicolas17"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-02-20T23:37:01.545Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-02-21T01:13:37.782Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 206530500,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 9836,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1286041458,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "We have Qt5 runners, but qsizetype exists starting with Qt 5.10 (just not as the return type for a QList), and on some compilers qsizetype and int are the same.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
